rth"},{"text":"மகள்","lemma":"மகள்","gloss":"daughter/woman"}],"gloss":"Earth-maiden"},{"surface":"அழுத","parts":[{"text":"அழு","lemma":"அழு","gloss":"to weep"},{"text":"த","lemma":"த","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"wept"},{"surface":"காஞ்சியும்","parts":[{"text":"காஞ்சி","lemma":"காஞ்சி","gloss":"instability/Kāñci"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"coordinating particle"}],"gloss":"and the Kāñci"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"உண்டு","gloss":"exists"}],"gloss":"exists"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"to say"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"உரைப்பரால்","parts":[{"text":"உரை","lemma":"உரை","gloss":"to say"},{"text":"ப்ப்","lemma":"ப்ப்","gloss":"future marker"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"அர்","gloss":"third person plural suffix"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"ஆல்","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"they say indeed"},{"surface":"உணர்ந்திசினோரே","parts":[{"text":"உணர்","lemma":"உணர்","gloss":"to understand"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ந்து","gloss":"past marker"},{"text":"இசின்","lemma":"இசின்","gloss":"euphonic particle"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"pronominal suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"those who have understood"}]}],"literal":"The dark, cloud-laden sky being her face, / the moving two luminaries named as her eyes, / the vast space where wind does not blow and movement is rare, / with a diamond-hubbed, shining-gem-spoked, / golden wheel rolled in the front of battle, / by kings of great strength in battle who found no rivals, / even though those ancestors have gone, without going herself, still / like women of price, claimed by many, / 'I exist, may you live, I!' saying, many times / the Earth-maiden wept, and this Kāñci / exists, so say indeed those who have understood.","translation":"With the dark, cloud-filled sky as her face, and the sun and moon as her eyes, the Earth stretches into the windless, pathless heights of space. Great kings of old, who rolled their golden chariot wheels with diamond hubs and gem-studded spokes into battle, finding no rivals to match their immense strength, have all departed. Yet, she does not go with them. Like a courtesan shared by many, she remains, saying to each new ruler, 'I am yours, may you live long!' Realizing her own plight, the Earth-maiden weeps. Those of deep wisdom say that this is the true nature of Kāñci—the realization of the world's transience.","modern":"மேகங்கள் சூழ்ந்த கரிய வானத்தை முகமாகவும், இயங்குகின்ற சூரிய சந்திரர்களைக் கண்களாகவும் கொண்டு, காற்று வீசாத விண்வெளி வரை பரந்து விரிந்தவள் நிலமகள். வைரத்தாலான அச்சினையும், விளங்கும் மணிகள் பதித்த ஆரங்களையும் கொண்ட பொன்னாலான தேருருளையை போர்க்களத்தில் உருட்டி, தமக்கு நிகரான பகைவரைக் காணாத வலிமை மிக்க அரசர்கள் பலர் இறந்துபோயினர். அவ்வாறு முன்னோர் பலர் சென்றபோதிலும், தான் அழியாமல் இன்னும் நிலைபெற்றிருக்கும் இந்நிலமகள், விலைமகளிரைப் போலப் பலராலும் உரிமை கொண்டாடப்படுகிறாள். 'நான் இன்னும் இருக்கிறேன், நீ வாழ்க!' என்று ஒவ்வொரு புதிய அரசனிடமும் கூறி, தன் நிலையை எண்ணிப் பலமுறை அழுது வருந்துகிறாள். உலகத்தின் இந்த நிலையாமையை உணர்த்தும் காஞ்சித் திணை உண்மையானது என்று அறிவுடையோர் கூறுவர்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and the theme of Peruṅkāñci, which reflects on the transience of life and worldly power. The poet Mārkkaṇṭēyaṉār personifies the Earth as a grand maiden whose face is the sky and whose eyes are the sun and moon. He describes how mighty kings of the past, who ruled with unmatched strength and rode golden chariots, have all perished and departed. Yet, the Earth remains behind, never leaving with them. Instead, she is passed from one ruler to another like a courtesan claimed by many men, offering herself to each new king. Realizing the sorrow of her own eternal but shared existence, the Earth-maiden weeps, illustrating the ultimate instability of human possession.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.9],